shoot:description:Baby bird season continues with a Western Kingbird nest I came across, up in a transmission tower.  This was a new part of town for this bird for me, so I was excited to find them there.  I also moved my bird bath, and took the opportunity to use my 200mm EF lens to photograph some regulars there (the female House Finch, and the Lesser Goldfinches).  Other young birds include the Red-breasted Sapsucker and Cooper's Hawk, though the hawk is probably old enough to not be considered a "baby bird."
