2026-07-15-094700-44-R5PT0991-LrC-AI-Remove-sm.jpg:description:I used Lightroom Classic's "Remove" feature with the "use generative AI" box checked to remove a small stick near the bird's head.
2026-07-15-094700-44-R5PT0991-sm.jpg:description:I used Lightroom Classic's "Remove" without AI, and a few masks and cloned areas.  It was a lot more work to remove the little stick.  I'm not sure if photo metadata saying "AI was used" will be a concern in the future, but I'm worried it may disqualify photos (someday) that are uploaded to eBird or iNaturalist or elsewhere.  I'm not sure whether to use AI to make minor cleanup faster or not.  On the other hand, the entire photo was run through DxO PureRAW.
